        ecrm:P3_has_note    "At the end of the 18th century embroidery designs began to develop into rigid and heavily stylised borders predominantly used on towels and napkins. A bath wrap was made from three widths of fabric and was used to wrap around the body while resting in the hamman [public baths] after bathing."@en ;
